%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 79f35638ac6885c4e955fbd2fef5cfba, type: 3}
  m_Name: ScrollbookDatabase
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ScrollbookDatabase
  characters:
  - title: Bits
    icon: {fileID: -8848074254060127402, guid: d218e8ff1ca6dcf41851c9a8f937f5e5, type: 3}
    description: An average pixel who wants to unite Spritz back together after the
      wiz'd destruction. His skill, Bit Buff, allows him to take less damage from
      obstacles by half.
  - title: Thief
    icon: {fileID: 1136184288765050124, guid: aa8710ef7a9076849874a1f9a7b1f50d, type: 3}
    description: A self-proclaimed thief, yet he doesn't really steal anything. He's
      a laid-back gentleman who is the great grandson of the founder of greenwood,
      and is currently the watcher of the town. His skill, Sticky Fingers, lets him
      pull in coins in a nearby radius.
  - title: Ninja
    icon: {fileID: 61506194941554554, guid: 500f72fcd9b34894ea6fc359fe580c69, type: 3}
    description: A quick-witted woman who silently sneaks where she travels. Working
      as one of several ninjas from ninja valley, her electric bolts were created
      by the high traces of voltage between her fingers, which she learned to control.
      Her skill, Electric Bolt, lets her fire a projectile to take out any obstacle.
  - title: Wiz Kid
    icon: {fileID: 694068958173167402, guid: a13018d0373c22e4e9bc72555eebd8a2, type: 3}
    description: A wizard who is still in training, trying to become a wizard like
      his father. Or...before his father went mentally unstable due to his anger.
      He may be a timid child, but as he tries controlling his powers, he'll one
      day master them. His skill, Sprouting Sorcery, lets his randomly restore amounts
      of energy.
  - title: Crystal
    icon: {fileID: -8710684726290518427, guid: ad90941f2e2de8e4291e9e7bf289c835, type: 3}
    description: A woman who was frozen in frosty outpost during the great war. When
      the war concluded, the idea of revenge excited her enough to shatter the glacier
      she was trapped in. Mysteriously, she gained the power to control wind and
      freezing temperatures, and she roams the world for her attacker, not knowing
      he's already gone. Her skill, Glaciate, is charged with snowflakes, and lets
      her freeze obstacles in a circle around her.
  - title: Cubit
    icon: {fileID: 377528032064278403, guid: 058659ad0ffe58248a063b9eb665c510, type: 3}
    description: It's unknown exactly how cubit made his way onto spritz. All that
      is known is that he's from a place with lots of platforming, and the atoms
      alligned incorrectly, transporting him here. His skill, Protection Protocol,
      lets him stop his energy depletion and store incoming damage for a short time,
      then restore his energy with said damage.
  obstacles:
  - title: Spikes
    icon: {fileID: 7145198348311737387, guid: f73dfe034c22cfc41bd7e8799020a5ac, type: 3}
    description: Spikes are a common obstacle with only one way to avoid them, and
      that's by jumping over them. They deal 15 damage and have no secondary effects.
  - title: Aliens
    icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: a8166ea434d337349818825bff42d2f6, type: 3}
    description: Aliens are an uncommnon obstacle with only one way to avoid them,
      and that's by jumping over them. They deal 15 damage and move faster than spikes.
  - title: Slimes
    icon: {fileID: -1207516536243021827, guid: 669d02063a8fc58438fea9a7a71d9e25, type: 3}
    description: There are three kinds of slimes, Green, Red, and Blue slimes. They
      each provide debuffs in they come in contact with the player, Green Slimes
      inflict the Sticky debuff, Red Slimes inflict Burning, and Blue Slimes inflict
      Soggy. Sticky - Lowers jump force by half. Burning - Take 5 damage for a couple
      of seconds. Soggy - Forces input delay for jumping and sliding. Green slimes
      deal 15 damage, and Red and Blue slimes deal 20 damage.
  - title: Magic Bolts
    icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 9687b8cba872c4f50aeb3b2b3ff1a0b7, type: 3}
    description: 'There are four kinds of magic bolts, each one having a chance to
      inflict the Curse debuff, and also have different behaviors in a level. Magic
      and Twin Bolts deal 15 damage, with the Twin Bolt having a 50/50 chance to
      deal half damage or double damage. Charged and Spark Bolts deal 20 damage. '
  spritzHistory:
  - title: The World of Spritz
    icon: {fileID: -4851718564733221013, guid: ac5a007d2c6d7a641b294f3c6f24fcbe, type: 3}
    description: Spritz is a planet in the Pixelverse, which was created by a fusion
      of pixels that gave every Sprite life. For the first hundreds of of years,
      the world was quiet, until five people came together to build communities of
      different cultures. These people became known as the founders of Pixelville,
      Greenwood, Ninja Valley, Frosty Outpost, and Wizardspeak. Life was simple,
      and everyone was happy. One day, these communities sought out for more resources,
      which led to pilfering amongst themselves...leading into the Great War. Sprites
      were killed ad injured left and right, and parts of Spritz were damage beyond
      recognition - Wizardspeak being the only named town to be affected. Realizing
      the fighting was becoming unstable, the founders called for a meeting, leading
      to the peace treaty to end the great war.
  founders:
  - title: Founder of Pixelville
    icon: {fileID: 15890179032266369, guid: e2bb8738977dab94ba9c2194812bce80, type: 3}
    description: 'Axiom Byte, known as the architect of order, was the one who figured
      out how to organize the chaotic pixel energy of spritz into stable structures,
      being the reason civilization exists at all. He''s a logical, calm visonary,
      who belived structure gave prosperity to people. He''s not very emotional,
      but deeply cared in a quiet way. '
  - title: Founder of Greenwood
    icon: {fileID: -907721790803237427, guid: c99abf2f37418384686a5790aac6e7c5, type: 3}
    description: 'Sylro Vex, known as the silent hand, built greenwood as a hidden,
      self-sufficient settlement, who taught his people how to take what they needed
      without being seen. He''s clever, resourceful, and secretive, but he was charming
      when he needed to be. He considered surval to be greater than rules in the
      grand scheme of things. '
  - title: Founder of Ninja Valley
    icon: {fileID: -4162772872327981196, guid: dabc574330200e84a88274fcb96ecb59, type: 3}
    description: 'Kairi Shin, known as the veiled guardian, created ninja valley
      as a place of training and spritual balance. Her women served as protectors
      untl the war made them all choose sides. She''s disciplined, honorable, and
      quiet, and she values balance and self-control. She speaks very little, but
      when she does, her voice matters. '
  - title: Founder of Frosty Outpost
    icon: {fileID: -1816940465327449870, guid: 30d320b8d7fc8024ab1980f3d4cc0519, type: 3}
    description: Eiran Glaciel, known as the heart of ice, built frosty outpost in
      the harshest region, mastering preservation of resources. He's elegant, composed,
      and emotionally guarded, and he values preservation and endurance, but he was
      kind in a distant way.
  - title: Founder of Wizardspeak
    icon: {fileID: 5698218290411745946, guid: d3ed3e37b9559f54ab1079484c00d66e, type: 3}
    description: Orin Lux, known as the first spellbinder, discovered how to manipulate
      raw pixel energy into magic, which lead to Wizarrdspeak becoming the center
      of knowledge and power. He is curious, eccentric, and imaginative, and is always
      experimenting. After the great war, he changed his name to "The Wiz" as an
      alias
  - title: Flaws
    icon: {fileID: 7561238145954236011, guid: 681f18d42825f7c40ab718fdde8bc653, type: 3}
    description: 'Each of the founders were not perfect. They had flaws that lead
      to the great war.

      Axiom Byte - Structures society, which caused inequality.

      Sylro
      Vex - Normalized stealing resources from others outside of Greenwood.

      Kairi
      Shin - Stayed neutral for too long when fighting began.

      Eiran Glaciel
      - Hoarded supplies and refused to give out any to other towns.

      Orin
      Lux - Introduced unstable magic, which soon became illega.l'
